        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk3-phrases-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Combine and repeat phrase structures",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Repeated numeral-classifier phrases can distribute items one by one. Paired 不A不B descriptions require compatible established words; an apposition names the same referent twice. A verb-complement phrase can expand with an object and quantity while remaining a predicate.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "一个一个地来。",
                "pinyin": "yī gè yī gè de lái 。",
                "meaning": "Come one at a time.",
                "audio": "5d3ebee6c88a1dbb84758d2004e2823ca785c09488ddcb00806ca98591e95ff6"
              },
              {
                "text": "他不高不矮。",
                "pinyin": "tā bù gāo bù ǎi 。",
                "meaning": "He is neither tall nor short.",
                "audio": "925e2c53da3759eb8d8da2b8382ef0b331d33932dce8a479684612767f11ab5b"
              },
              {
                "text": "我的朋友小王来了。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ de péngyou xiǎowáng lái le 。",
                "meaning": "My friend Xiao Wang has arrived.",
                "audio": "a9518afae8fde1a952b12be5425e3d768cb1cfa9e3bd20940d179c6e8983522d"
              },
              {
                "text": "我看完三本书了。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ kàn wán sān běn shū le 。",
                "meaning": "I have finished reading three books.",
                "audio": "7efb34149b6d5a2cb18134a44cbc0cbdbfa6fb3b0219c2c88e1a7bd42b91ecbc"
              }
            ]
